### What is a URL shortener and what is its traffic shape?

A URL shortener maps a long URL to a short, unique code and redirects any request for that code back to the original URL. There are two operations: create (rare) and redirect (extremely frequent). The system is therefore read-heavy by a huge ratio, so the redirect path must be as cheap as possible.

```java
package com.bank.shortener.model;

import java.time.Instant;

public class UrlMapping {
    private String shortCode;   // e.g. "aB3xK9"
    private String longUrl;     // e.g. "https://nbi.com/offers/home-loan?campaign=2024"
    private String owner;       // e.g. "marketing-team"
    private Instant createdAt;
    private Instant expiresAt;
    private long clickCount;

    // Constructor and getters omitted for brevity
}
```

### How does counter plus base62 code generation work?

Take a globally unique, ever-increasing number and encode it in base62 (digits 0-9, A-Z, a-z). Uniqueness is guaranteed by construction, so there are zero collisions.

```java
package com.bank.shortener.service;

public class Base62Encoder {

    private static final String ALPHABET =
        "0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz";

    public static String encode(long number) {
        if (number == 0) return "0";
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        while (number > 0) {
            sb.append(ALPHABET.charAt((int) (number % 62)));
            number /= 62;
        }
        return sb.reverse().toString();
    }

    public static long decode(String code) {
        long result = 0;
        for (char c : code.toCharArray()) {
            result = result * 62 + ALPHABET.indexOf(c);
        }
        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long id = 123456789L;
        String code = encode(id);
        System.out.println("Encoded: " + code);
        System.out.println("Decoded: " + decode(code));
    }
}
```

